# Arguments passed to `python -m ui.main` by the epaper-ui service.
#
#   --display auto      LCD HAT when fitted, PNG frames otherwise
#   --input auto        HAT buttons when available, keyboard otherwise
#                       (under systemd stdin is closed, so keyboard input
#                       is simply inactive - the UI still renders)
#   --interval 60       seconds between panel refreshes for patterns that
#                       do not set their own pace (flash wear)
#
# Options worth adding for a show or a battery run:
#
#   --locked            ignore the buttons, so a knock cannot stop the
#                       demo (unlock: KEY2 KEY3 KEY2; it re-locks itself
#                       after a minute of quiet)
#   --blank-after 10    blank the backlight after 10 s idle, worth about
#                       20-40 mA. Off by default; any press wakes it.
#   --no-standby        skip the startup white-out and leave the factory
#                       autoplay running until a demo is started
#
# On startup the UI stops the boards' factory autoplay and paints every
# sector white - that is the agreed idle state for the installation.
#
UI_ARGS=--display auto --input auto --interval 60 --frames /tmp/epaper-ui
